{
  "version": 3,
  "note": "The single source of truth for dietary preferences: the profile form (via /api/preferences), the plan prompt, and the post-generation check are all built from this file. 'excludesTags' is matched against a catalog item's own tags in data/prices.json and is exact — it is how a known ingredient is judged, and it is why adding a catalog item never means editing a list of names here. 'forbids' is the word-level net for free text with no catalog entry: a cooking step, or an ingredient the catalog has never heard of. 'allows' phrases are removed before 'forbids' is matched, so 'peanut butter' does not trip dairy-free's 'butter'. Word matching is boundary-safe and plural-tolerant: 'egg' catches 'eggs' but never 'eggplant'. 'group' places the option in the profile form; 'note' explains an option the Tempe catalog cannot enforce, so it never looks broken. A bad or empty file makes the server refuse to start, by design.",
